 "interpretation_notes": [
  "Central Station rows: the daily pages print 'Sunrise'/'Sunset' with no place; the explanation page says sunrise and sunset are given for the adopted Central Station. That attribution is IMD's text, not an inference.",
  "City rows: the tables page prints 18 time cells per row under the headers Chennai, Delhi, Kolkata, Mumbai, each with Sun and Moon Rise/Set. The page header did not align with the cells in the tool output. Mapping used (Claude's inference, to be confirmed by QA's own read): cells 1-2 Chennai Sun rise/set, 5-6 Delhi Sun, 9-10 Kolkata Sun, 13-14 Mumbai Sun (cells 3-4, 7-8, 11-12, 15-16 are the Moon). It is supported by the values themselves (for example Delhi 05:24/19:23 on 22 June, the USNO Delhi value on 21 June is 05:24/19:22) and by every Moon cell pattern ('- -' only in Moon columns).",
  "The city coordinates IMD used for the tables page are not printed there; the correction-page coordinates (arcminute precision, about 4 s of time per arcminute of longitude) are assumed.",
  "Times are IST (UTC+05:30), printed to the minute; the rounding rule is not stated. One Chaitra day-1 value is printed '6:02 AM'/'6:12 PM', the rest 'h. 6-01'/'h. 18-12'; both are recorded as HH:MM."
